 # Carnot — Operational Status
 
-**Last Updated:** 2026-09-03
+**Last Updated:** 2026-09-04
+
+## 2026-09-04 — Quarantine stamps measured against the current rule (two operator decisions)
+
+An hourly outer-loop check re-ran `adversarial_verify.verify_artifact` over every
+artifact that carries a `flagged_adversarial` stamp. A stamp quarantines an
+artifact: capstones and headline tasks must skip it.
+
+Measured, 2026-09-04 21:15Z, read-only (no artifact was written):
+
+- 6,030 artifacts scanned in `results/`. 410 carry a stamp.
+- **43 of those 410 (10.5%) raise no critical flag under the current rule.**
+- 367 still raise one. The two largest kinds are `DURATION_TOO_SHORT` (243) and
+  `TAUTOLOGY` (189).
+
+The 43 are not evidence of a broken gate. They are artifacts whose stamp was
+written when the rule was narrower, and the rule has since widened. Three of them
+landed today (exp6965, exp6967, exp6972); all three declare a deterministic,
+non-model substrate and now resolve to a 0.0001s duration floor instead of the
+60s live-inference floor.
+
+**This state is already adjudicated. Do not re-derive it.** Exp6172
+(`results/experiment_6172_current_rule_quarantine_determination.json`) settled the
+policy: the stamp is immutable history, the artifact stays quarantined, and
+`operator_reopen_required=true`. What is new here is only the count — 43 — which
+was not known before.
+
+**OPERATOR DECISION 1 (new).** Whether to reopen any of the 43 for headline or
+capstone use. Reopening is operator-only per exp6172. The list is reproducible by
+re-running the scan; it was not persisted, because writing it into `results/` would
+itself be a record edit.
+
+**OPERATOR DECISION 2 (new).** Exp6979 (`self_learning_cold_audit`) still flags
+today, and correctly by the linter's own logic. It declares
+`inference_substrate: fresh_process_readonly_transaction_replay`. That name matches
+neither escape hatch the verifier offers: it has no `deterministic` leading token,
+and no `_no_llm` name suffix. So it falls to the 60s live-model floor at a real
+duration of 0.029s.
+
+The fix is not to add the name to the verifier's allowlist. That allowlist has grown
+by one constant per incident for months, and adding a name to make a check pass is
+forbidden. The fix belongs in the task prompt: an agent writing a non-model substrate
+must use one of the legal values, or follow the `_no_llm` suffix convention that the
+verifier already recognizes by pattern. Whether to make that a planner-prompt change
+is the operator's call.
+
